{"id": "EUVD-2026-101214", "enisaUuid": "2f8eb2e3-801b-3cef-b30d-44695380a35f", "description": "OW2 ASM 3.0 before 9.11 contains a quadratic memory allocation vulnerability in MethodWriter.computeMaxStackAndLocal() and computeAllFrames() when using COMPUTE_MAXS or COMPUTE_FRAMES. Attackers can supply a crafted class file with thousands of overlapping exception handlers, causing excessive Edge allocations and an OutOfMemoryError that crashes the JVM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T00:59:41", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/merge_requests/461", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/commit/91057c98239d994aed5e46434e34e00d593c0daf", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/blob/ASM_9_10_1/asm/src/main/java/org/objectweb/asm/MethodWriter.java#L1662", "https://asm.ow2.io/versions.html", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ow2-asm-3.0-before-9.11-quadratic-memory-allocation-via-exception-handlers"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f8m6-wmrx-8vh2", "CVE-2026-110260"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2ea65b90-a15a-36a0-a4e4-911be29110b6", "product": {"name": "ASM", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}, "product_version": "3.0 <9.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8ba49a8c-f981-31de-8396-9ef86b2022b8", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}], "isExploited": false}